AUDIO: 'Welcome back to Vantage with AI. I\'ve been a bit preoccupied over the last week, and just when I was about to finish the next video I\'ve been working on, one of my viewers pointed me toward this little nugget in the Creal 2 ecosystem. So, I thought, why not do a quick addendum to the series and cover'

[00:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'this instead? A big thank you to AI Infictados for bringing it to my attention. If you\'ve been following this series, you\'ll know that one of Creal 2\'s biggest limitations has been image editing. While the workflow we covered in the previous video could use multiple'

[00:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'reference images to guide generation, it wasn\'t a true image editing solution and couldn\'t reliably preserve a person\'s identity. That changes with today\'s project. We\'re taking a look at Creal 2 Identity Edit, a community-developed'

[00:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Laura that adds instruction-based image editing to Creal 2. Instead of simply using reference images as guidance, this Laura lets you provide an image along with an editing instruction and attempts to modify only the parts you\'ve asked'

[00:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'for while preserving everything else. What\'s even more interesting is that the project is evolving very quickly. The V1 release came out just a few days ago, and they have already released V1.1, which is now the recommended version.'

[01:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'According to the release notes, it brings significant improvements to face likeness, object removal and replacement, outfit changes, and handling multiple people. The only notable regression is that person replacement edits, such as replacing a'

